{"video_id": "vR2q7at97Cs", "channel_id": "UCHmfoIM7gE05O4bhkgPY1Mg", "fetched_at": "2026-11-25T04:12:56.602795+00:00", "fetch_tool": "yt-dlp 2026.08.19", "caption_track_type": "auto_generated", "segments": [{"start_seconds": 0.16, "end_seconds": 4.24, "text": "Hello, welcome to my channel. In this"}, {"start_seconds": 2.4, "end_seconds": 6.72, "text": "video, I'm going to cover all the"}, {"start_seconds": 4.24, "end_seconds": 9.36, "text": "details of how to implement Firebase"}, {"start_seconds": 6.72, "end_seconds": 11.04, "text": "messaging into a Flutter project, send"}, {"start_seconds": 9.36, "end_seconds": 13.92, "text": "and receive remote messages from"}, {"start_seconds": 11.04, "end_seconds": 16.56, "text": "Firebase, and display notifications on"}, {"start_seconds": 13.92, "end_seconds": 18.56, "text": "Android and especially is devices for"}, {"start_seconds": 16.56, "end_seconds": 23.0, "text": "both cases when the app is in the"}, {"start_seconds": 18.56, "end_seconds": 23.0, "text": "foreground and background states."}, {"start_seconds": 23.26, "end_seconds": 26.42, "text": "[Music]"}, {"start_seconds": 26.88, "end_seconds": 32.56, "text": "To start, let's create a new Firebase"}, {"start_seconds": 29.8, "end_seconds": 36.08, "text": "project and type a sample name for it"}, {"start_seconds": 32.56, "end_seconds": 36.08, "text": "like push notification"}, {"start_seconds": 37.64, "end_seconds": 43.04, "text": "sample. Since we don't need Gemini, we"}, {"start_seconds": 40.4, "end_seconds": 43.04, "text": "can disable"}, {"start_seconds": 43.24, "end_seconds": 47.36, "text": "it as well as Google"}, {"start_seconds": 54.68, "end_seconds": 60.0, "text": "Analytics. Once the project is created"}, {"start_seconds": 57.2, "end_seconds": 62.48, "text": "on Firebase, go to your flatter project,"}, {"start_seconds": 60.0, "end_seconds": 65.12, "text": "open terminal and add Firebase core"}, {"start_seconds": 62.48, "end_seconds": 67.16, "text": "plug-in. We also need Firebase messaging"}, {"start_seconds": 65.12, "end_seconds": 68.96, "text": "plug-in to receive push"}, {"start_seconds": 67.16, "end_seconds": 71.12, "text": "notifications for displaying"}, {"start_seconds": 68.96, "end_seconds": 75.28, "text": "notifications in the foreground. Add"}, {"start_seconds": 71.12, "end_seconds": 75.28, "text": "flatter local notification plug-in as"}, {"start_seconds": 76.68, "end_seconds": 82.48, "text": "well. Now, all three plugins that are"}, {"start_seconds": 79.6, "end_seconds": 85.52, "text": "needed were added into pubspec yaml file"}, {"start_seconds": 82.48, "end_seconds": 88.44, "text": "with the latest versions. I'm going to"}, {"start_seconds": 85.52, "end_seconds": 91.28, "text": "use Firebase command line interface or"}, {"start_seconds": 88.44, "end_seconds": 93.36, "text": "CLI. It will significantly speed up the"}, {"start_seconds": 91.28, "end_seconds": 95.44, "text": "process of dealing with Firebase"}, {"start_seconds": 93.36, "end_seconds": 97.76, "text": "services. If you haven't installed it,"}, {"start_seconds": 95.44, "end_seconds": 98.84, "text": "check the official documentation on how"}, {"start_seconds": 97.76, "end_seconds": 102.32, "text": "to do"}, {"start_seconds": 98.84, "end_seconds": 103.86, "text": "this by typing Firebase login. Check if"}, {"start_seconds": 102.32, "end_seconds": 105.64, "text": "you are"}, {"start_seconds": 103.86, "end_seconds": 110.64, "text": "[Music]"}, {"start_seconds": 105.64, "end_seconds": 110.64, "text": "authenticated. Now activate flatterfire"}, {"start_seconds": 113.36, "end_seconds": 118.8, "text": "[Music]"}, {"start_seconds": 115.88, "end_seconds": 121.52, "text": "CLI to configure flatter app to connect"}, {"start_seconds": 118.8, "end_seconds": 125.04, "text": "to already created Firebase project."}, {"start_seconds": 121.52, "end_seconds": 125.04, "text": "Type flatter fire"}, {"start_seconds": 127.0, "end_seconds": 131.44, "text": "configure. Select the project that you"}, {"start_seconds": 129.28, "end_seconds": 134.44, "text": "have previously created on Firebase"}, {"start_seconds": 131.44, "end_seconds": 134.44, "text": "console."}, {"start_seconds": 135.28, "end_seconds": 139.76, "text": "Make sure that Android and iOS are"}, {"start_seconds": 141.96, "end_seconds": 147.6, "text": "selected. Firebase plug-in has created"}, {"start_seconds": 144.8, "end_seconds": 150.96, "text": "and configured Android and iOS"}, {"start_seconds": 147.6, "end_seconds": 154.96, "text": "applications on Firebase console and"}, {"start_seconds": 150.96, "end_seconds": 157.8, "text": "fetched Google service info.pl file for"}, {"start_seconds": 154.96, "end_seconds": 161.04, "text": "iOS module and Google"}, {"start_seconds": 157.8, "end_seconds": 163.36, "text": "services.json file for Android. Now"}, {"start_seconds": 161.04, "end_seconds": 165.84, "text": "let's open Apple developer account to"}, {"start_seconds": 163.36, "end_seconds": 167.08, "text": "create a PNS key. Here you need to click"}, {"start_seconds": 165.84, "end_seconds": 169.48, "text": "on"}, {"start_seconds": 167.08, "end_seconds": 173.12, "text": "account. Select"}, {"start_seconds": 169.48, "end_seconds": 175.84, "text": "keys and let's create a new APNS key for"}, {"start_seconds": 173.12, "end_seconds": 180.92, "text": "push notifications. Enable Apple push"}, {"start_seconds": 175.84, "end_seconds": 182.96, "text": "notification service. Add name and click"}, {"start_seconds": 180.92, "end_seconds": 185.92, "text": "configure. Because it's a sample"}, {"start_seconds": 182.96, "end_seconds": 188.32, "text": "project, it's okay to use one APNS key"}, {"start_seconds": 185.92, "end_seconds": 191.12, "text": "for both development and production"}, {"start_seconds": 188.32, "end_seconds": 195.28, "text": "environments. However, it's recommended"}, {"start_seconds": 191.12, "end_seconds": 195.28, "text": "that you use a separate key for each"}, {"start_seconds": 197.08, "end_seconds": 202.24, "text": "environment. Once the key is configured,"}, {"start_seconds": 199.52, "end_seconds": 203.4, "text": "click register and download the key. We"}, {"start_seconds": 202.24, "end_seconds": 206.16, "text": "will need it"}, {"start_seconds": 203.4, "end_seconds": 210.36, "text": "later. Now, let's get back to Firebase"}, {"start_seconds": 206.16, "end_seconds": 213.96, "text": "console to add created APNS key for the"}, {"start_seconds": 210.36, "end_seconds": 217.2, "text": "project. Select project"}, {"start_seconds": 213.96, "end_seconds": 220.48, "text": "settings, cloud messaging tab. Scroll"}, {"start_seconds": 217.2, "end_seconds": 223.04, "text": "down to Apple app configuration section"}, {"start_seconds": 220.48, "end_seconds": 225.6, "text": "and upload APNS key that you have"}, {"start_seconds": 223.04, "end_seconds": 228.64, "text": "downloaded from Apple developer account."}, {"start_seconds": 225.6, "end_seconds": 231.0, "text": "You also need to specify APNS key ID and"}, {"start_seconds": 228.64, "end_seconds": 234.08, "text": "your Apple developer team"}, {"start_seconds": 231.0, "end_seconds": 236.2, "text": "ID. Both of them you can find on Apple's"}, {"start_seconds": 234.08, "end_seconds": 238.8, "text": "developer"}, {"start_seconds": 236.2, "end_seconds": 242.72, "text": "account. After adding IDs, let's"}, {"start_seconds": 238.8, "end_seconds": 244.64, "text": "complete uploading of APNS key."}, {"start_seconds": 242.72, "end_seconds": 247.2, "text": "Now it's time to configure iOS"}, {"start_seconds": 244.64, "end_seconds": 249.76, "text": "application in Xcode. If you are using"}, {"start_seconds": 247.2, "end_seconds": 252.72, "text": "Android Studio ID, you can select iOS"}, {"start_seconds": 249.76, "end_seconds": 255.56, "text": "folder. Then go to tools flatter and"}, {"start_seconds": 252.72, "end_seconds": 259.92, "text": "select open iOS module in"}, {"start_seconds": 255.56, "end_seconds": 262.8, "text": "Xcode. In Xcode ID, select runner runner"}, {"start_seconds": 259.92, "end_seconds": 265.24, "text": "target. Go to sign in and capabilities"}, {"start_seconds": 262.8, "end_seconds": 267.36, "text": "tab and click on new"}, {"start_seconds": 265.24, "end_seconds": 270.08, "text": "capability. Search for push"}, {"start_seconds": 267.36, "end_seconds": 272.2, "text": "notifications and click to add it. We"}, {"start_seconds": 270.08, "end_seconds": 275.04, "text": "also need to add background modes"}, {"start_seconds": 272.2, "end_seconds": 277.36, "text": "capability that lets the application to"}, {"start_seconds": 275.04, "end_seconds": 280.0, "text": "respond to incoming push notifications"}, {"start_seconds": 277.36, "end_seconds": 283.36, "text": "even when it's not actively running in"}, {"start_seconds": 280.0, "end_seconds": 286.88, "text": "the foreground. Once it's added, enable"}, {"start_seconds": 283.36, "end_seconds": 286.88, "text": "remote notifications for this"}, {"start_seconds": 287.48, "end_seconds": 293.04, "text": "capability. By default, if the app is in"}, {"start_seconds": 290.48, "end_seconds": 296.48, "text": "terminated state, Firebase messaging"}, {"start_seconds": 293.04, "end_seconds": 298.4, "text": "plug-in will show a notification. But if"}, {"start_seconds": 296.48, "end_seconds": 301.12, "text": "the app is in the foreground"}, {"start_seconds": 298.4, "end_seconds": 302.88, "text": "notification won't be displayed. That's"}, {"start_seconds": 301.12, "end_seconds": 305.2, "text": "why we are going to use flatter local"}, {"start_seconds": 302.88, "end_seconds": 306.84, "text": "notifications plug-in for showing"}, {"start_seconds": 305.2, "end_seconds": 309.36, "text": "foreground"}, {"start_seconds": 306.84, "end_seconds": 312.16, "text": "notifications. We need to create service"}, {"start_seconds": 309.36, "end_seconds": 315.2, "text": "classes for both firebased messaging and"}, {"start_seconds": 312.16, "end_seconds": 317.56, "text": "local notifications plugins. Create a"}, {"start_seconds": 315.2, "end_seconds": 321.04, "text": "new directory in the lip"}, {"start_seconds": 317.56, "end_seconds": 322.68, "text": "folder and create dart file for flatter"}, {"start_seconds": 321.04, "end_seconds": 325.68, "text": "local notification"}, {"start_seconds": 322.68, "end_seconds": 328.0, "text": "service. Since we need one instance of"}, {"start_seconds": 325.68, "end_seconds": 330.72, "text": "local notification service, let's"}, {"start_seconds": 328.0, "end_seconds": 333.2, "text": "implement a single turn pattern by using"}, {"start_seconds": 330.72, "end_seconds": 336.0, "text": "private constructor static final"}, {"start_seconds": 333.2, "end_seconds": 339.72, "text": "instance and factory constructor that"}, {"start_seconds": 336.0, "end_seconds": 339.72, "text": "returns instance."}, {"start_seconds": 355.35, "end_seconds": 358.51, "text": "[Music]"}, {"start_seconds": 363.62, "end_seconds": 370.29, "text": "[Music]"}, {"start_seconds": 372.64, "end_seconds": 375.78, "text": "[Music]"}, {"start_seconds": 378.61, "end_seconds": 386.69, "text": "[Music]"}, {"start_seconds": 397.24, "end_seconds": 400.24, "text": "Hey,"}, {"start_seconds": 405.24, "end_seconds": 409.24, "text": "hey, hey."}, {"start_seconds": 411.35, "end_seconds": 419.42, "text": "[Music]"}, {"start_seconds": 422.24, "end_seconds": 430.44, "text": "[Music]"}, {"start_seconds": 432.79, "end_seconds": 435.92, "text": "[Music]"}, {"start_seconds": 438.76, "end_seconds": 446.82, "text": "[Music]"}, {"start_seconds": 471.49, "end_seconds": 479.55, "text": "[Music]"}, {"start_seconds": 482.37, "end_seconds": 489.96, "text": "[Music]"}, {"start_seconds": 484.68, "end_seconds": 489.96, "text": "Hey, hey, hey."}, {"start_seconds": 490.61, "end_seconds": 506.32, "text": "[Music]"}, {"start_seconds": 504.32, "end_seconds": 508.72, "text": "To complete configuring flatter local"}, {"start_seconds": 506.32, "end_seconds": 512.64, "text": "notifications plug-in, we need to adjust"}, {"start_seconds": 508.72, "end_seconds": 515.8, "text": "a bit native iOS main function."}, {"start_seconds": 512.64, "end_seconds": 518.44, "text": "Open Xcode. Click on"}, {"start_seconds": 515.8, "end_seconds": 522.96, "text": "runner. Select runner"}, {"start_seconds": 518.44, "end_seconds": 522.96, "text": "folder and open app delegate"}, {"start_seconds": 523.48, "end_seconds": 527.92, "text": "file. Import flatter local"}, {"start_seconds": 528.12, "end_seconds": 533.76, "text": "notifications and add the following"}, {"start_seconds": 530.4, "end_seconds": 536.08, "text": "piece of code."}, {"start_seconds": 533.76, "end_seconds": 539.92, "text": "The first one tells Flatter to connect"}, {"start_seconds": 536.08, "end_seconds": 542.32, "text": "notifications plug-in to the iOS system."}, {"start_seconds": 539.92, "end_seconds": 545.44, "text": "And the second one ensures iOS can"}, {"start_seconds": 542.32, "end_seconds": 549.56, "text": "handle notifications and pass events"}, {"start_seconds": 545.44, "end_seconds": 552.08, "text": "like tabs back to Flatter by using the"}, {"start_seconds": 549.56, "end_seconds": 556.84, "text": "plug-in. More information you can find"}, {"start_seconds": 552.08, "end_seconds": 556.84, "text": "on their page on Pop Dev."}, {"start_seconds": 557.89, "end_seconds": 561.04, "text": "[Music]"}, {"start_seconds": 563.04, "end_seconds": 567.6, "text": "Now let's get back to flatter project"}, {"start_seconds": 565.2, "end_seconds": 570.6, "text": "and create service for firebase"}, {"start_seconds": 567.6, "end_seconds": 570.6, "text": "messaging."}, {"start_seconds": 576.03, "end_seconds": 582.56, "text": "[Music]"}, {"start_seconds": 585.64, "end_seconds": 592.22, "text": "[Music]"}, {"start_seconds": 606.21, "end_seconds": 609.29, "text": "[Music]"}, {"start_seconds": 612.68, "end_seconds": 616.68, "text": "Hey, hey, hey."}, {"start_seconds": 618.1, "end_seconds": 621.16, "text": "[Music]"}, {"start_seconds": 623.53, "end_seconds": 626.65, "text": "[Music]"}, {"start_seconds": 629.49, "end_seconds": 637.56, "text": "[Music]"}, {"start_seconds": 662.22, "end_seconds": 670.28, "text": "[Music]"}, {"start_seconds": 673.08, "end_seconds": 681.29, "text": "[Music]"}, {"start_seconds": 683.64, "end_seconds": 686.78, "text": "[Music]"}, {"start_seconds": 689.63, "end_seconds": 697.69, "text": "[Music]"}, {"start_seconds": 722.35, "end_seconds": 730.42, "text": "[Music]"}, {"start_seconds": 733.24, "end_seconds": 759.74, "text": "[Music]"}, {"start_seconds": 758.24, "end_seconds": 762.79, "text": "Everything."}, {"start_seconds": 759.74, "end_seconds": 762.79, "text": "[Music]"}, {"start_seconds": 765.16, "end_seconds": 768.28, "text": "[Music]"}, {"start_seconds": 771.13, "end_seconds": 779.19, "text": "[Music]"}, {"start_seconds": 792.56, "end_seconds": 799.44, "text": "Now it's time to set usage of both"}, {"start_seconds": 795.32, "end_seconds": 799.44, "text": "services. So open main"}, {"start_seconds": 799.72, "end_seconds": 803.56, "text": "file. Check if the binding is already"}, {"start_seconds": 802.48, "end_seconds": 806.96, "text": "set"}, {"start_seconds": 803.56, "end_seconds": 810.0, "text": "up. Initialize Firebase application with"}, {"start_seconds": 806.96, "end_seconds": 813.12, "text": "default Firebase options. This is the"}, {"start_seconds": 810.0, "end_seconds": 814.74, "text": "class that was generated by Flutterfire"}, {"start_seconds": 813.12, "end_seconds": 817.9, "text": "CLI."}, {"start_seconds": 814.74, "end_seconds": 817.9, "text": "[Music]"}, {"start_seconds": 819.36, "end_seconds": 826.4, "text": "Use instance factory to get local"}, {"start_seconds": 821.68, "end_seconds": 826.4, "text": "notification service and call init"}, {"start_seconds": 827.0, "end_seconds": 833.04, "text": "method. Similarly, get firebase"}, {"start_seconds": 829.84, "end_seconds": 835.28, "text": "messaging service and call init method"}, {"start_seconds": 833.04, "end_seconds": 837.16, "text": "by you need to pass the instance of"}, {"start_seconds": 835.28, "end_seconds": 839.44, "text": "local notification"}, {"start_seconds": 837.16, "end_seconds": 841.92, "text": "service. Now it's time to run the"}, {"start_seconds": 839.44, "end_seconds": 845.08, "text": "project and get test notifications from"}, {"start_seconds": 841.92, "end_seconds": 845.08, "text": "the Firebase."}, {"start_seconds": 846.48, "end_seconds": 853.91, "text": "[Music]"}, {"start_seconds": 854.88, "end_seconds": 858.08, "text": "Allow notifications"}, {"start_seconds": 858.12, "end_seconds": 863.12, "text": "permission and after that you will see"}, {"start_seconds": 860.72, "end_seconds": 865.92, "text": "push notification token in the logs"}, {"start_seconds": 863.12, "end_seconds": 868.92, "text": "which you should copy and go to Firebase"}, {"start_seconds": 865.92, "end_seconds": 868.92, "text": "console."}, {"start_seconds": 875.6, "end_seconds": 879.92, "text": "Find run dropdown and select"}, {"start_seconds": 881.24, "end_seconds": 886.32, "text": "messaging. Click on create your first"}, {"start_seconds": 883.64, "end_seconds": 889.84, "text": "campaign. Select Firebase notification"}, {"start_seconds": 886.32, "end_seconds": 893.28, "text": "messages and click on create. Write"}, {"start_seconds": 889.84, "end_seconds": 893.28, "text": "notification title and"}, {"start_seconds": 893.8, "end_seconds": 900.16, "text": "text. Click send test message. And here"}, {"start_seconds": 898.16, "end_seconds": 902.64, "text": "you need to add push notification token"}, {"start_seconds": 900.16, "end_seconds": 903.72, "text": "that you have copied from the logs in"}, {"start_seconds": 902.64, "end_seconds": 907.36, "text": "your"}, {"start_seconds": 903.72, "end_seconds": 910.0, "text": "IDE. Once you click on test, Firebase"}, {"start_seconds": 907.36, "end_seconds": 912.56, "text": "will send a notification to your device."}, {"start_seconds": 910.0, "end_seconds": 914.88, "text": "The app was in the foreground state. So"}, {"start_seconds": 912.56, "end_seconds": 918.0, "text": "the notification was displayed by using"}, {"start_seconds": 914.88, "end_seconds": 920.32, "text": "flatter local notifications plug-in. Now"}, {"start_seconds": 918.0, "end_seconds": 923.76, "text": "let's try another case when the app is"}, {"start_seconds": 920.32, "end_seconds": 925.96, "text": "closed or in a terminated state."}, {"start_seconds": 923.76, "end_seconds": 930.64, "text": "modify a bit"}, {"start_seconds": 925.96, "end_seconds": 930.64, "text": "title and send test notification"}, {"start_seconds": 931.4, "end_seconds": 936.16, "text": "again. You see that the background"}, {"start_seconds": 933.6, "end_seconds": 938.72, "text": "notification was displayed even if the"}, {"start_seconds": 936.16, "end_seconds": 938.72, "text": "app was"}, {"start_seconds": 940.44, "end_seconds": 945.52, "text": "closed. To summarize, we have used"}, {"start_seconds": 942.8, "end_seconds": 948.24, "text": "Firebase messaging plug-in for receiving"}, {"start_seconds": 945.52, "end_seconds": 950.16, "text": "remote messages from Firebase and"}, {"start_seconds": 948.24, "end_seconds": 952.32, "text": "displaying notifications when the app is"}, {"start_seconds": 950.16, "end_seconds": 954.64, "text": "terminated."}, {"start_seconds": 952.32, "end_seconds": 956.96, "text": "When the app is not terminated, flatter"}, {"start_seconds": 954.64, "end_seconds": 959.0, "text": "local notifications plug-in triggers"}, {"start_seconds": 956.96, "end_seconds": 961.12, "text": "logic for display"}, {"start_seconds": 959.0, "end_seconds": 963.6, "text": "notifications. For most cases is"}, {"start_seconds": 961.12, "end_seconds": 965.84, "text": "absolutely enough. However, if you need"}, {"start_seconds": 963.6, "end_seconds": 968.64, "text": "more customizations, it's possible to"}, {"start_seconds": 965.84, "end_seconds": 970.96, "text": "use local notifications plug-in for"}, {"start_seconds": 968.64, "end_seconds": 973.6, "text": "showing notifications for both cases"}, {"start_seconds": 970.96, "end_seconds": 976.24, "text": "when the app is terminated and when the"}, {"start_seconds": 973.6, "end_seconds": 978.64, "text": "app is in the foreground state. But this"}, {"start_seconds": 976.24, "end_seconds": 981.24, "text": "is a topic for another video."}, {"start_seconds": 978.64, "end_seconds": 983.52, "text": "The code works for both Android and iOS"}, {"start_seconds": 981.24, "end_seconds": 985.92, "text": "applications. Almost no changes were"}, {"start_seconds": 983.52, "end_seconds": 988.6, "text": "needed for Android because Flutterfire"}, {"start_seconds": 985.92, "end_seconds": 990.72, "text": "CLI did it"}, {"start_seconds": 988.6, "end_seconds": 993.28, "text": "automatically. The link to the code you"}, {"start_seconds": 990.72, "end_seconds": 995.84, "text": "can find in the video description. Hope"}, {"start_seconds": 993.28, "end_seconds": 997.92, "text": "that this tutorial was helpful for you."}, {"start_seconds": 995.84, "end_seconds": 1000.64, "text": "Feel free to share your thoughts and"}, {"start_seconds": 997.92, "end_seconds": 1003.35, "text": "questions in the comments. And for now,"}, {"start_seconds": 1000.64, "end_seconds": 1006.72, "text": "thanks for watching. See you next time."}, {"start_seconds": 1003.35, "end_seconds": 1006.72, "text": "[Music]"}]}